ev('EVD064',"Echo 2 on the night of the log (analysis/warren_echo2_passes.py, from SAO mean elements; the two element sets agree to ~10 s): three visible passes over Cheyenne on 1 Aug 1965 UTC — P1 0502-0508Z (peak 10 deg, E->NE), P2 0650-0659Z (peak 66 deg, az 118->97->14: rising ESE, peaking in the east, ending N), P3 0839-0848Z (peak 25 deg, W->NNW). In printed-clock terms: H0 Mountain 2302/0050/0239 MDT; H1 EST 0002/0150/0339; H2 EDT 0102/0250/0439. Echo 1 has no visible pass in the window (its only geometric pass, ~0321-0335Z, precedes it).",'ANALYST_CALCULATION','SRC038; analysis/warren_echo2_passes.py, warren_echo1_passes.py','INC033;EXP032;EVD063','8834','HIGH','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
ev('EVD065',"Coincidence with log entries (analysis/warren_echo2_coincidence.py): with +-3 min slack, H0 matches 1 entry (2:50), H1 matches 3 (1:48, 1:49, 3:40), H2 matches 3 (2:50, 3:00, 4:40 [a call time]). A random shift of the clock gives a mean of 1.9 of 18 entries inside pass windows (P(>=3) ~ 0.26), so the Echo 2 matches are NOT significant. Qualitatively: under H1 the 1:48-1:49 'same formation at G and E flights' coincides with P2's rise in the ESE and 3:40 sits in P3 but P3 runs W->N, not 'heading west'; under H2 '2:50 nine more UFOs' and '3:00 white oval directly overhead' coincide with P2 (peak 66 deg, east), which is a better fit to 'overhead' than Deneb only if the observer judged 66 deg as overhead.",'ANALYST_CALCULATION','analysis/warren_echo2_coincidence.py','INC033;EXP032','8834','HIGH','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
ev('EVD066',"Echo 2 cannot explain the log's multi-object or crossing-motion entries: it is a single object crossing the sky in ~5-9 visible minutes at ~0.1-0.3 deg/s, silent, steady, brightness ~ +1 to +2.5. It is a candidate for isolated 'moving light' entries only. Printy's review lists Echo 1/2 and other satellites as generators of reports across the whole Aug 1965 flap; that is plausible but, for Warren, unproven.",'ANALYST_ASSESSMENT','analysis; SRC034','INC033;EXP032','8834','MEDIUM','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
ev('EVD067',"Quality note (self-correction): my first run of the satellite scripts used the wrong sign when converting MJD to PyEphem dates, which put the Sun ~90 days off in the sunlit/dark tests; I found it because the printed Sun altitude was implausible, fixed it, and all results above are from the fixed version (Sun alt -24 deg at 05Z, -31 deg at 07Z, -25 deg at 09Z). Positions use Keplerian propagation of mean elements (no short-period terms): tens of km.",'METHODOLOGICAL_NOTE','analysis scripts','INC033','8834','LOW','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
